repository-code: 'https://github.com/apparebit/shantay'
repository-artifact: 'https://pypi.org/project/shantay/'
abstract: >-
  Shantay is a command line tool for analyzing the EU's Digital Services Act
  Transparency Database. Said database collects so-called statements of reasons
  for each content moderation decision by internet platforms and search engines.
  In contrast to the EU's own tooling, which isn't developed in the open and is
  targeted at cluster environments, Shantay is designed to run on consumer-level
  hardware. A consumer laptop with a suitably large external drive suffices,
  with the first two years of statements taking up almost 2T. Shantay downloads
  daily distributions, extracts comprehensive statistics either for the entire
  database or a topic-specific subset, and visualizes those statistics in HTML
  reports.
